{"ts": "2026-08-17T12:56:15Z", "agent": "claude", "seq": 101, "kind": "message", "text": "Now I have full context: no backend delete-related tests to preserve beyond what exists, no conflicting backlog items, and the CSS/component conventions are clear. I'll write the spec as a frontend-only feature \u2014 an optimistic-hide-plus-timer undo pattern that never actually needs to reconstruct a deleted task, since nothing is sent to the server until the undo window lapses.", "meta": {"native_type": "assistant", "block_type": "text", "session_id": "5664dabf-122c-4fdb-aaf7-26ca2b27fb0a"}}
{"ts": "2026-08-17T12:56:41Z", "agent": "claude", "seq": 102, "kind": "tool_use", "text": "Write", "meta": {"native_type": "assistant", "block_type": "tool_use", "tool_use_id": "toolu_01LtkXCFtyvXLumy6EeCLGsq", "input": {"file_path": "/home/dev/projects/test-project/docs/spec.md", "content": "# Spec: Let me undo deleting a task\n\n**Taiga:** #13\n**Type:** Feature\n**Branch:** feature/tp-13/let-undo-deleting-task\n\n## Goal\n\nWhen I delete a task, give me a few seconds to change my mind and get it\nback exactly as it was \u2014 including whether it was marked done \u2014 instead of\nthe delete being instant and final.\n\n## Design decision: frontend-only, no backend changes\n\nDelete stays hidden from the list immediately, but the actual `DELETE\n/api/tasks/{id}` request is deferred for a 5-second undo window instead of\nfiring right away. If the window lapses with no undo, the request fires then,\nexactly as today. If Undo is clicked, the deferred request is simply never\nsent and the task's row is un-hidden.\n\nThis means the task's local state (`title`, `done`, `priority`, `due_date`)\nis never mutated or removed from `App.jsx`'s `tasks` array during the undo\nwindow \u2014 it is only filtered out of what's rendered. So \"exactly as it was\"\nis automatic, not something to reconstruct: undo can't get any field wrong\nbecause nothing was ever changed. This also avoids touching `backend/`,\n`store.py`, or `api.js` at all \u2014 the existing `DELETE /api/tasks/{id}`\nroute and 404-on-missing behavior (`backend/app/main.py:69`) are reused\nunmodified.\n\nRejected alternative: a backend soft-delete/trash + restore endpoint. It\nwould need new routes, TTL bookkeeping, and lazy-expiry logic in\n`store.py`, for the same end result \u2014 ruled out because it spans the data\n+ interface layers for no behavioral gain over the frontend-only approach\n(see \"Split work that spans layers\" \u2014 this keeps the cycle to one layer).\n\n**Undo window: 5 seconds.** (Open question below \u2014 proceeding with this as\nthe default.)\n\n## Acceptance criteria\n\n1. **Given** a task in the list, **when** I click Delete, **then** the task\n   disappears from the list immediately (list and open/done counts both\n   exclude it) and an undo notice appears showing the task's title and an\n   \"Undo\" button.\n2. **Given** the undo notice is showing for a task, **when** I click Undo\n   before the window elapses, **then** the task reappears in the list with\n   the exact same id, title, priority, due date, and done state it had\n   before \u2014 no `DELETE` request was ever sent.\n3. **Given** the undo notice is showing and I take no action, **when** 5\n   seconds elapse, **then** the `DELETE` request is sent (task is\n   permanently gone) and the notice disappears on its own.\n4. **Given** a completed (done) task, **when** I delete it and then click\n   Undo, **then** it reappears still marked done \u2014 not reset to open.\n5. **Given** I delete two different tasks before either window elapses,\n   **when** I click Undo on one, **then** only that task is restored; the\n   other's countdown and eventual delete are unaffected.\n6. **Given** a task is pending deletion, **when** its window elapses and the\n   `DELETE` request 404s because the task was already removed some other\n   way in the meantime (e.g. \"Clear completed\" ran during the window),\n   **then** no error is shown to the user.\n\n## Non-goals\n\n- No change to backend delete semantics \u2014 once committed, a delete is still\n  immediate and permanent; there is no server-side trash or restore\n  endpoint.\n- No undo for the \"Clear completed\" bulk action \u2014 out of scope for this\n  ticket, which is about the single-task Delete button.\n- No cross-session or cross-reload undo. If the tab is closed or refreshed\n  during the undo window, the deferred delete never fires (task simply\n  reappears on next load, since the backend never received it) \u2014 this is\n  accepted as-is, not treated as a bug to fix.\n- No keyboard shortcut (e.g. Ctrl+Z) for undo \u2014 button click only.\n- No configurable undo duration \u2014 5 seconds, fixed.\n\n## Affected areas\n\n- `frontend/src/App.jsx` \u2014 owns `tasks` state; needs a `pendingDeleteIds`\n  set (or map of id \u2192 timeout handle) so `stateFiltered`/`visibleTasks`/\n  `sortedTasks` and the `completedCount`/`openCount` derivations\n  (`App.jsx:31-47`) exclude pending-delete tasks; owns starting/cancelling\n  the 5s timer and firing `api.deleteTask` on expiry with 404 swallowed.\n- `frontend/src/components/TaskList.jsx` \u2014 `onDelete` currently calls\n  `api.deleteTask` straight through via `App.jsx:82`'s `run()` wrapper; this\n  needs to change to the new deferred-delete flow instead of an immediate\n  `run(() => api.deleteTask(id))`.\n- `frontend/src/components/UndoToast.jsx` \u2014 new component, one file per the\n  existing per-component convention (sibling of `ClearCompleted.jsx`,\n  `TaskCounts.jsx`). Renders one row per pending delete: task title + Undo\n  button. Needs `aria-live`/`role=\"status\"`, matching the existing\n  `.empty`/`.error` accessibility pattern (`TaskList.jsx:24`,\n  `App.jsx:65`).\n- `frontend/src/App.css` \u2014 new styles for the undo notice; no existing\n  toast/banner styling to reuse beyond `.error`'s color pattern.\n- No changes to `backend/`, `frontend/src/api.js`, or `frontend/src/main.jsx`.\n\n## Edge cases\n\n- **Filtered/searched view**: deleting a task that's currently visible under\n  a filter/search still removes it from view and starts its undo window;\n  Undo restores it as normal even though the row was never re-fetched (it\n  was only hidden, not removed from state).\n- **Empty-state text during a pending delete**: if the deleted task was the\n  last visible one, the \"Nothing to do yet\" / filter-specific empty message\n  appears immediately even though an undo is still possible \u2014 this is\n  intended, not a bug, and follows directly from \"disappears immediately.\"\n- **Two pending deletes, one undone**: covered by acceptance criterion 5 \u2014\n  each pending delete tracks its own timer independently; no shared/most-\n  recent-only undo slot.\n- **Delete race with \"Clear completed\"**: covered by acceptance criterion 6\n  \u2014 a 404 on the deferred delete must be swallowed silently, not surfaced\n  via `setError`.\n- **Rapid double Undo click / click after expiry**: once the window elapses\n  the notice and Undo button are removed together with the pending-delete\n  entry, so there's no stale button to double-click into an inconsistent\n  state.\n- **Delete during an in-progress title edit**: not applicable \u2014 Delete and\n  Edit are mutually exclusive actions on a row already (Edit swaps to a\n  form; the row must be in its non-editing state to see the Delete button\n  at all per `TaskList.jsx:71-99` vs `101-145`), so no new interaction here.\n\n## Open questions\n\n- **Undo window length.** No duration was specified in the ticket (\"a\n  brief chance\"). Proceeding with **5 seconds**, a common convention for\n  this exact pattern (e.g. Gmail's send-undo). Override before build if a\n  different duration is wanted.\n"}, "session_id": "5664dabf-122c-4fdb-aaf7-26ca2b27fb0a"}}
